 ### Reference map
 
+The tables that follow state the value the cascade declares for each token, and
+`tests/src/styles/tokens.test.ts` resolves every stated value against the built cascade in each
+mode. Every value cell states a value: one code span for each token the row's first cell names,
+`` `light`, dark `dark` `` where a table's single value column carries the light and the dark
+reading together, or `the same expression` where the dark scope repeats the light cell. The
+`collectReferenceRows` reader in `tests/setupStyles.ts` refuses a cell written in any other form,
+so a law about a scale belongs in a sentence beside its table rather than in a cell. A `Role` cell
+names the role whose fill the row gives, so that row's token is the role's own
+`--vn-color-{role}-base`. A `Tier` row is a template over `{role}` and `{fill}`, and it expands over
+every role the preceding table names.
+
+The styles build shortens a number and a duration, so a stated value and the declaration are
+compared with every number written in full and every millisecond duration written in seconds. A
+percentage compares as its own number written in full, so `15%` and `15.0%` compare equal and `16%`
+does not. The build also rewrites a color channel into the engine's own serialization, so a pair
+that differs as text is compared again as the color each side paints.
+
